abstract: >-
  We establish unconditionally that no system of 59 equiangular lines exists in
  R^18, narrowing N(18) to {57, 58}. In dimension 19, we prove unconditionally that
  74 equiangular lines exist in R^19 if and only if there exists a strongly
  regular graph SRG(75, 32, 10, 16); combined with the theorem of Azarija and
  Marc (2018), this yields N(19) <= 73 and narrows N(19) to {72, 73}. The proof
  combines an exact mod-2^(n+1) Pfaffian congruence for odd-order Seidel matrices,
  unique odd-order Eulerian switching laws, generalized Galois orthogonality over
  simple spectral factors, De Caen-Jacobi resolvent analysis, a frozen 56-file
  exact integer/rational certificate archive, and a Lean 4 formalization (v4.36.0,
  127 kernel-audited declarations on standard axioms).
